		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<span class="comment-author-name">Sherry Bare</span> <span class="says">says</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">February 18, 2025 at 8:56 am</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p><img class="wprm-comment-rating" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODdhAQABAPAAAP///wAAACwAAAAAAQABAEACAkQBADs=" data-lazy-src="https://cooktoria.com/wp-content/plugins/wp-recipe-maker/assets/icons/rating/stars-5.svg" alt="5 stars" width="80" height="16" /><br />
Very delicious! I love colour so added some red bell pepper. Added Onion to the Sautéed Cabbage and cut back the amount of cabbage to make it more hearty for my hubby. He's not a fan of too many carrots so just did a quarter of these. I stirred in Chopped cilantro and green onions instead of parsley. Very nice indeed. Thank you so much for sharing with us.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-62367" data-commentid="62367" data-postid="870" data-belowelement="article-comment-62367" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Sherry Bare" aria-label="Reply to Sherry Bare">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	<ul class="children">

	<li class="comment byuser comment-author-taniasheff bypostauthor odd alt depth-2" id="comment-62385">
	<article id="article-comment-62385">

		
		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<span class="comment-author-name">Tania Sheff</span> <span class="says">says</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">February 20, 2025 at 12:53 pm</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p>Thanks, Sherry! I love your variation of the recipe!</p>
		</div>

